.TH DUPMAP 1 "September 2026" "dupmap 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dupmap \- terminal disk usage treemap and duplicate report
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dupmap
.RI [ options ] [ path ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dupmap
recursively scans a directory and displays its contents as a navigable
terminal treemap. Small files are grouped in a navigable \fBother\fR folder.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dupes [path]
Report duplicate files and estimated reclaimable space, then exit.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Show the program version.
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Select an item.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected directory.
.TP
.B Backspace
Return to the parent directory.
.TP
.B l
Toggle the complete list view.
.TP
.B f
Enter a filename filter in list view.
.TP
.B s
Cycle size, name, and modified-time sorting.
.TP
.B c
Cycle depth, file-type, and size-heat colors.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH FILESYSTEM BEHAVIOR
Symbolic links are skipped and are never followed. Directories that cannot be
read are displayed as inaccessible instead of terminating the scan.
.SH STATE
When no path is supplied, the last directory and display modes are loaded from
the dupmap state file under XDG_STATE_HOME, or ~/.config/dupmap/state.
